<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.Africa money mkt shortage climbs to 9.4 bln rand.</title>
<headline>S.Africa money mkt shortage climbs to 9.4 bln rand.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Reserve Bank said the South African money market shortage climbed to 9.383 billion rand on Monday from 8.956 billion rand on Saturday.</p>
<p>On the money market, banks quoted their three-month NCD rates unchanged at between 16.95 percent and 17.00 percent offered, while the 90-day BA rate was also steady at between 16.30 and 16.60 percent.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
